        <item rdf:about="https://www.nature.com/articles/s41467-026-77618-6">
            <title>[9] Berry curvature multipoles in Kagome superconductor CsV3Sb5</title>
            <link>https://www.nature.com/articles/s41467-026-77618-6</link>
            <content:encoded><![CDATA[<p><b>Last authors:</b> Xu Han, Kian Ping Loh</p><p><b>Authors:</b> Shanshan Liu, Prasun Boyal, Enze Zhang, Qifeng Hu, Xu Han, Kian Ping Loh</p><p><span style='display:inline-block;padding:4px 9px;border-radius:999px;background:#fee2e2;color:#991b1b;font-weight:700;'>Score 9/10</span> <b>A_MUST_READ</b></p><p><b>Why:</b> title strong match: kagome superconductor</p><p><b>Tags:</b> <span style='display:inline-block;margin:2px 4px 2px 0;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:999px;background:#eef2ff;color:#3730a3;font-size:12px;'>#kagome</span> <span style='display:inline-block;margin:2px 4px 2px 0;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:999px;background:#eef2ff;color:#3730a3;font-size:12px;'>#CsV3Sb5</span> <span style='display:inline-block;margin:2px 4px 2px 0;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:999px;background:#eef2ff;color:#3730a3;font-size:12px;'>#V3Sb5</span> <span style='display:inline-block;margin:2px 4px 2px 0;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:999px;background:#eef2ff;color:#3730a3;font-size:12px;'>#nematic</span> <span style='display:inline-block;margin:2px 4px 2px 0;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:999px;background:#eef2ff;color:#3730a3;font-size:12px;'>#Berrycurvature</span> <span style='display:inline-block;margin:2px 4px 2px 0;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:999px;background:#eef2ff;color:#3730a3;font-size:12px;'>#superconduct</span></p><p><img src='https://pubads.g.doubleclick.net/gampad/ad?iu=/285/nature_communications/article&amp;sz=728x90&amp;c=-2005641609&amp;t=pos%3Dtop%26type%3Darticle%26artid%3Ds41467-026-77618-6%26doi%3D10.1038/s41467-026-77618-6%26techmeta%3D119,120,126,128,142,144%26subjmeta%3D1003,1064,1130,119,2795,301,357,639,766,995%26kwrd%3DElectronic+properties+and+materials,Phase+transitions+and+critical+phenomena,Superconducting+devices,Superconducting+properties+and+materials' style='max-width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:10px;' /></p><hr/><p><b>Abstract:</b> Higher-order nonlinear Hall responses can reveal Berry-curvature multipoles associated with electronic nematicity. Here, the authors identify a vortex-enhanced third-order Hall response in CsV3Sb5 and uncover a Berry-curvature quadrupole associated with chiral loop-current order</p>]]></content:encoded>
