        <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Last authors:&lt;/b&gt; Xu Han, Kian Ping Loh&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Authors:&lt;/b&gt; Shanshan Liu, Prasun Boyal, Enze Zhang, Qifeng Hu, Xu Han, Kian Ping Loh&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style='display:inline-block;padding:4px 9px;border-radius:999px;background:#fee2e2;color:#991b1b;font-weight:700;'&gt;Score 9/10&lt;/span&gt; &lt;b&gt;A_MUST_READ&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Why:&lt;/b&gt; title strong match: kagome superconductor&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Tags:&lt;/b&gt; &lt;span style='display:inline-block;margin:2px 4px 2px 0;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:999px;background:#eef2ff;color:#3730a3;font-size:12px;'&gt;#kagome&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style='display:inline-block;margin:2px 4px 2px 0;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:999px;background:#eef2ff;color:#3730a3;font-size:12px;'&gt;#CsV3Sb5&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style='display:inline-block;margin:2px 4px 2px 0;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:999px;background:#eef2ff;color:#3730a3;font-size:12px;'&gt;#V3Sb5&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style='display:inline-block;margin:2px 4px 2px 0;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:999px;background:#eef2ff;color:#3730a3;font-size:12px;'&gt;#nematic&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style='display:inline-block;margin:2px 4px 2px 0;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:999px;background:#eef2ff;color:#3730a3;font-size:12px;'&gt;#Berrycurvature&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style='display:inline-block;margin:2px 4px 2px 0;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:999px;background:#eef2ff;color:#3730a3;font-size:12px;'&gt;#superconduct&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src='https://pubads.g.doubleclick.net/gampad/ad?iu=/285/nature_communications/article&amp;amp;sz=728x90&amp;amp;c=-2005641609&amp;amp;t=pos%3Dtop%26type%3Darticle%26artid%3Ds41467-026-77618-6%26doi%3D10.1038/s41467-026-77618-6%26techmeta%3D119,120,126,128,142,144%26subjmeta%3D1003,1064,1130,119,2795,301,357,639,766,995%26kwrd%3DElectronic+properties+and+materials,Phase+transitions+and+critical+phenomena,Superconducting+devices,Superconducting+properties+and+materials' style='max-width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:10px;' /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;hr/&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Abstract:&lt;/b&gt; Higher-order nonlinear Hall responses can reveal Berry-curvature multipoles associated with electronic nematicity. Here, the authors identify a vortex-enhanced third-order Hall response in CsV3Sb5 and uncover a Berry-curvature quadrupole associated with chiral loop-current order&lt;/p&gt;</description></item>
    
